      AND model_answer IS NOT DISTINCT FROM 'Malignant Hyperthermia (MH) is a rare, life-threatening pharmacogenetic hypermetabolic disorder of skeletal muscle. It is primarily inherited in an autosomal dominant fashion, involving mutations in the RYR1 (ryanodine receptor) gene on chromosome 19, which leads to uncontrolled calcium release from the sarcoplasmic reticulum.

